ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.5.md:194:## Adapter behavior and the L6 fence
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.5.md:196:`allocate_observation_buffers` writes the29 shapes/dtypes in the copied inventory and constructs **existing** `KaggricultureObsBatch` and `KaggricultureActionMask`. Build exact named NumPy views once in an internal typed `NativeArrays` holder; it mirrors binding parameters, not another policy schema. All tensor storage retained. **Outputs:** each of the 35 output NumPy views is created once at allocation and reused; no per-step `.numpy()` on outputs, shape inference, reward recalculation or returned NumPy allocations. **Inputs (rereview item 4):** `step` and `truncate_envs` receive fresh caller tensors each call, so after the checks below the adapter takes exactly one zero-copy `.numpy()` view per call of `actions.tokens`, `actions.lengths` and the truncate `mask`, passes it to native and drops it on return. The view shares the tensor's storage (`view.__array_interface__['data'][0] == tensor.data_ptr()`, tested); no `np.asarray` copy, `.contiguous()`, `.cpu()`, dtype cast or cached input view. Allocate the six transition tensors once and pass all 35 keywords explicitly to1.4. Fail requested pinning if allocator unavailable; CPU tests pass pin_memory=False. Orbit behavior is unchanged.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.5.md:231:Encode/decode wrappers serialize/parse canonical JSON once and call1.4's exact bindings. Full batch helpers are **cold paths** (fixtures/BC/replay); return CPU int64 rows. Derive actor count only from this seat's `actor_mask[..., :241]`, order_limit from obs.order_limits, hire_limit from action_spec. No rival-private input, hidden state or synthetic length0 live rows. Preserve list order, EMPTY `[]`, market0, omitted vs positive explicit unit quantities. Reject missing farmer/hands/market, extra hands, None insertion, bool/string quantities, dirty tail, unsupported layout/version. Existing G grammar performs those checks. `encode_action_into` is atomic on failure; batch helper fills newly allocated private output and returns only if all rows succeed.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.5.md:252:3.1 may assume exact buffer/stub contract, explicit seed rule, synchronous autoreset, strict CPU actions, native grammar tables, reward config and the entry fence exist. It may not assume trainer GAE/storage/evaluation/model factory already supports Kaggriculture. Synthetic-table default in the model is the only model integration1.5 owns; model factory/compile dispatch stays3.1. 3.6 alarm already exists but its Kaggriculture/multirank behavior needs tests (W:python/owl/train/ppo.py:1113,1157–1185; W:cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:17).
