cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:11:# Kaggriculture BC trainer warm-starts PPO from the held-out best
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:13:Plan Task 5.2 asks for a BC trainer on the rebuilt model that reuses Isaiah's optimizer factory, BF16 and compile path, keeps the best checkpoint by held-out NLL and stops on sustained held-out degradation (lesson L9). This change builds the trainer script and its tests. The BC run itself waits for the Task 5.1 shards and the pod.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:17:- `scripts/train_bc.py`: CLI in `run_ppo.py`'s shape (fresh `CONFIG --data --output-dir`, restart from a run directory, `torchrun` for several GPUs, `--log-mode`, `--wandb-mode online|offline`, `--max-runtime-hours`, `--source-commit`). It runs the GEMM workload check for the BC microbatch and validation forwards and the compile-stack check. It then builds the model with `create_model` and `reset_parameters`, compiles through `configure_model_compile` (the Kaggriculture cuBLAS-only claim), builds the optimizer with `create_optimizer` / `create_lr_scheduler` and wraps it with Isaiah's DDP adapter.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:18:- `python/owl/train/bc.py`: `BCConfig`, the objective, `TrainSharding`, `HeldOutSelection`, checkpoint and resume state, a W&B logger (project `kg-v3`, `job_type` `bc`) and `train_bc`. BF16 comes from the PPO config's `rl.dtype` through `autocast_context`. The model, dtype and compile settings come from the PPO config that BC warm-starts (`ppo_config`), so the BC checkpoint matches that PPO run's model. `wrap_bc_model_for_distributed` casts the model for Isaiah's Orbit-annotated DDP adapter, whose dispatch passes Kaggriculture batches through unchanged. The Task 3.1 trainer seam has not generalized those annotations yet.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:19:- `python/owl/kaggriculture/bc_data.py`: the shard writer and loader. `configs/bc/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml`: the 2-rank BC config for `configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml`. It sits under `configs/bc/` because the existing config tests load every top-level `configs/*.yaml` as a PPO `FullConfig`. `README.md` has a new "Kaggriculture BC warm start" section.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:23:- **The critic is trained, not frozen.** Isaiah trains all of the shared trunk and both heads together, and his teacher distillation weights policy KL and winner CE equally (`teacher_kl_coef = teacher_value_coef`). BC is distillation from the recorded player. So the loss is the turn NLL divided by program length, plus `value_coef` (1.0) times the per-seat winner CE against the episode's raw final banks (L1: the larger bank wins, a draw is 0.5 each). The reference froze the critic head, but its trunk still moved, so its critic reached PPO miscalibrated with no target. A test shows that a policy-only loss leaves the four `critic_head` tensors without gradients. Isaiah's adapter builds DDP without unused-parameter detection for this model, so the joint loss also gives every parameter a gradient. DDP itself was not run. Isaiah's own recipe used no imitation learning (`docs/write-up.md`); BC here is the plan's owner-required addition.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:24:- **Shard format.** The loader follows the refreshed 5.1 brief (branch `kg/rebuild-bc-brief` at `bcefd02`, still awaiting Codex review). Shards are `kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1`: one `np.savez_compressed` per episode at `<split>/<day>-<episode_id>.npz`, with the 28 observation fields, `can_act`, `tokens`, `lengths`, `turn` and a `schema` id. The brief lists the manifest's contents but not its key names. The loader requires `schema`, `observation_schema_version`, `contract_document_version` and per-episode `episode_id`, `split`, `terminal_banks`, `admitted`, `shard_path`, `shard_sha256` and `shard_bytes`. It keeps other custody keys uninterpreted. Task 5.1's `prepare.py` must emit these names, or use `write_bc_episode` / `write_bc_manifest`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:38:  - the 2-rank BC config targeting the 2-rank PPO config;
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:40:- Mutation checks (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.2/mutations.log`) killed 11 of 12 mutants. The survivor shares one permutation seed across ranks. The rank partitions are disjoint, so it changes no row set.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:41:- `just py-prepare`: 1,691 passed, 11 skipped, docs-fresh clean (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/5.2/py-prepare.log`).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best.md:46:- The BC run needs the 5.1 shards. Their token half waits on the Task 1.4 `kaggriculture_encode/decode` binding, and the full-slice run needs a machine that can read volume `4llk4uaf20`. It also needs the pod and FlashAttention, because `configs/model/kaggriculture.yaml` forces it (plan 6.0). PPO from the BC best then needs `run_ppo.py` to run Kaggriculture (Tasks 1.4/3.1). Today only its loaders are exercised.
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:62:- `docs/model-architecture.md` describes the protocol. It and the docstrings state the inherited `concat` behavior exactly: the first chunk's layout wins, a later chunk missing one of its optional targets raises, and a target carried only by later chunks is silently dropped. `python/owl/model/base.py` is untouched because another stream owns it.
cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:90:- **Orbit behaviour.** Orbit output is unchanged except in failure paths. When several optional fields mismatch, the copy error now names the first one in declaration order (`fleet_target` before `player_features`). The device-copy action-mask error now says `destination action-mask type mismatch` instead of `obs action-mask ...`. The alarm itself is new default-on behaviour for every Orbit config: a run that previously trained on corrupted replay now aborts.
cookbook/references/failed-training-reports-status-before-distributed-cleanup.md:46:  the behavior; the task brief and result receipt retain the local evidence.
cookbook/references/index.md:5:- [[kaggriculture-bc-trainer-warm-starts-ppo-from-the-held-out-best|Kaggriculture BC trainer warm-starts PPO from the held-out best]]: Task 5.2 trainer script on Isaiah's factory, optimizer, BF16, cuBLAS-only compile and DDP seams. It trains the critic with a raw-bank winner CE and reads the refreshed 5.1 `kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1` shards into rank-partitioned host memory. It keeps the held-out-NLL best in run_ppo's checkpoint schema and stops after sustained non-improvement (L9). 18 CPU tests on synthetic shards; no GPU, real-data or W&B execution; the run waits for 5.1 shards (Task 1.4 tokens) and the pod.
cookbook/references/index.md:26:- [[bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads|Native replay BC bootstrap]] — Market-disabled controls preserve3000 bank; exact admitted replay actions and Rust features support separate current-model BC, with episode holdout, two-rank smoke, observed overfitting and incomplete quality validation; automatic PPO disabled; BC stopped early for a separately requested PPO experiment, which then failed with a CUDA illegal memory access later traced to a compiler GEMM overflow; the planned architecture alignment schedules one BC rerun. Source review corrects omitted-unit handling: Python None is rejected, not encoded as NONE.
